Name: unregisterAllVoiceCommands

Type: command

Syntax: unregisterAllVoiceCommands

Summary:
Removes every registered voice command phrase. The speech recognition
engine will no longer match any phrases until new ones are registered.

Introduced: 1.0.0

OS: mac, Windows, Linux

Platforms: desktop

Example:
-- Clear all commands, then re-register only the ones needed in this context
unregisterAllVoiceCommands
registerVoiceCommand "next slide"
registerVoiceCommand "previous slide"

Example:
-- Clean up when a stack closes
on closeStack
    stopListening
    unregisterAllVoiceCommands
end closeStack

Description:
Use <unregisterAllVoiceCommands> to clear the entire voice command
registry in one call. This is equivalent to calling <unregisterVoiceCommand>
for every phrase that was registered, but more efficient.

The command does not stop the recognition engine — call <stopListening>
separately if you also want to stop listening.

References: registerVoiceCommand (command), unregisterVoiceCommand (command),
stopListening (command), voiceCommand (message)

Tags: speech, voice
